# Normalise line endings so Windows checkouts and the Linux CI runners agree.
# Text files are stored LF in the repository and checked out per-platform.
* text=auto

*.cs        text diff=csharp
*.csproj    text
*.sln       text eol=crlf

# **LF even on Windows, and this is a bug fix rather than a preference.** A shell script checked
# out CRLF works under Git Bash, which tolerates the carriage returns — and is a syntax error the
# moment the same file is read by a Linux bash, which is what happens whenever one of these is run
# in a container against a mounted Windows checkout. `tests/shell/kill-tree.test.sh` drives the
# Linux half of `scripts/e2e.sh`'s process handling and can only be run that way from here; it
# failed with `syntax error near unexpected token $'{\r'` until this line existed. Its own positive
# control is what caught it, which is the argument for having one.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.json      text
*.md        text
*.yml       text
*.yaml      text
*.editorconfig text
*.gitattributes text

# Binary — never touch these.
*.pdf       binary
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.ico       binary
